      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481876086": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates globally in the healthcare sector, focusing on improving health outcomes through technology. It addresses challenges related to healthcare access and equity by connecting individuals with care, pharmacy benefits, and data. The organization emphasizes diversity, inclusion, and health equity on a large scale.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe ASSOCIATE SOFTWARE ENGINEER role involves contributing to the development of healthcare portal features that support claims and insurance processing. The position is responsible for building backend services and enhancing web applications, leveraging modern technologies and AI tools to optimize performance and software delivery. This role plays a key part in advancing the organization's technology solutions that impact health services.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop healthcare portal features for claims and insurance.\nBuild Java backend services and RESTful APIs using Java, Spring Boot, and PostgreSQL.\nEnhance application performance and responsiveness across platforms.\nParticipate in requirements gathering, design, code reviews, and Agile delivery.\nMonitor and troubleshoot production applications using Splunk.\nDesign and deploy AI-powered solutions and automations.\nUtilize AI tools to streamline development workflows and improve delivery.\nDevelop event-driven components with Apache Kafka and AWS cloud services.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree.\nMinimum 1 year full-stack development experience with Java (17 or higher) and Spring Boot.\nMinimum 1 year experience with React and TypeScript for web applications.\nMinimum 1 year working with relational databases and SQL using PostgreSQL.\nMinimum 1 year experience with logging/monitoring tools (e.g., Splunk) and version control (e.g., Git).\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nSalary range is $60,200 to $107,400 annually for full-time employment.\nCompensation and benefits are influenced by factors such as location, education, and experience.\nBenefits & Perks:\n401(k) contribution and equity stock purchase options.\nComprehensive benefits package.\nIncentive and recognition programs.\nEqual Opportunity Statement:\nOur client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer."
        }
