      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481889336": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "<p><strong>Job Overview:</strong></p><p>You’ll work on our self-hosted LLM observability platform (built on Langfuse) — it’s where all our AI services send their traces, so we can see how every document and model call flows through the system, what it costs, and why things break. It’s a TypeScript/Node codebase running on Kubernetes (AKS). You’ll help build and operate the platform and the instrumentation around it — a great role for someone early-career who’s genuinely curious about how systems behave in production.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Job Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li>Instrumenting our services with traces, metrics, and structured logs, and making that data useful in dashboards and alerts.</li><li>Helping run and maintain the platform (web + worker services, and the queues and datastores behind them).</li><li>Triaging issues by following a request end-to-end through the traces.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>1–2 years of backend / platform / full-stack engineering or strong internship/project experience.</li><li>Solid programming in TypeScript/JavaScript (Node.js) — or strong fundamentals in another language with genuine willingness to ramp on TypeScript quickly.</li><li>Hands-on experience with at least one cloud provider (Azure, AWS, or GCP) and the basics of </li><li>compute and networking — with a willingness to go deeper fast.</li><li>Comfortable with Docker/containers (or eager to learn) and curious about Kubernetes.</li><li>Genuine interest in observability — you like understanding how requests flow and why things fail, and you’re comfortable reading logs, metrics, and traces.</li><li>Basic working knowledge of LLMs — what tokens, context windows, and quotas mean, and why tracing and cost-tracking matter for AI apps.</li><li>Good debugging instincts; comfortable with Git, REST/HTTP, and JSON.</li><li>Fluency with AI-assisted dev tools (Claude Code, Cursor, or similar), and a fast learner who likes to go deep.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Nice To Have:</strong></p><ul><li>Kubernetes/Helm, or any container-orchestration exposure.</li><li>OpenTelemetry, Langfuse, or distributed tracing experience.</li><li>Next.js / React, tRPC, Prisma, or BullMQ.</li><li>PostgreSQL, ClickHouse, or Redis.</li><li>Azure specifically (AKS, ACR, Key Vault, Front Door), or IaC (Terraform/Bicep).</li><li>CI/CD with GitHub Actions.</li></ul>"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483277694": {
